            "boundary": "CTB-106 completes the actual Color program-resource model and composes with CTB-99 through CTB-105 to qualify full canonical Color. Earlier mathematical bodies and raw/weak semantic hypotheses are unchanged. The shared measured right-fold preserves literal erasure, ordered callback states and noncommutative costs. Actual helper, construction, fixed-K selection and painting executions count Boolean/Option/control operations and operand-sensitive arithmetic; selection trajectories include the final residual, painting uses original adjacency and right-fold order. Successful lookup insertion attempts are counted separately from final used-color cardinality; successful suffix coloring proves actual writes rather than assuming them. The full normalized supplied-input bound is 64*P with P=n^2*b^2+n*D*b+D*(b+c)+(n+1)*k*c+n+1, b,c>=1, and stored/mentioned-key plus palette-color bit bounds. Graph construction charges original edge occurrences separately; palette setup and exports remain separately priced. Numeric decoders return actual decoded values and charge explicitly supplied fees; output list cells and pairs are counted. These are declared source events, not parser/byte-formatting, physical allocation/sharing/GC, machine arithmetic or wall-time bounds. All 18 prewritten case groups and 40 evaluations retain their expected results, including source selection 731, coloring 1058, separate exported pipeline 1584, padding counterfamilies and the 320*b^2 long-key bound. Shared semantic and SimpleGraph clients retain their actual validity, progress and palette hypotheses; no new provider/compiler equivalence is asserted. Full Color qualification is source qualification. FINAL/publication and receiving quality/whole-library acceptance remain mandatory; all remaining FDSA/PFDS work continues."
          }
